<article class="env-definition" id="020R">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/020R">Definition <span data-tag="020R">34.3.4</span>.</a> Compare Schemes, Definition <a href="/tag/01HT" data-tag="01HT">26.5.2</a>. Let $T$ be an affine scheme. A <em>standard Zariski covering</em> of $T$ is a Zariski covering $\{ U_ j \to T\} _{j = 1, \ldots , m}$ with each $U_ j \to T$ inducing an isomorphism with a standard affine open of $T$. </p>
